DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260728T193000
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=TU
SUMMARY:Family block\, no phones — Dinner: Curd Rice + Vathal Kuzhambu (W
 eek 4)
DESCRIPTION:Dinner (~6:30) + floor play or books\, her pick. Phone physical
 ly out of the room. Narrate\, expand her sentences\, offer one real choice
 .\n\nDINNER TONIGHT: Curd rice — mix 2 cups cooked rice (mashed slightly
 ) with 1.5 cups yogurt\, 1/2 cup milk\, salt. Temper 1 tsp mustard seeds\,
  curry leaves\, 1 dried red chili in 1 tbsp oil — mix in.\nVathal kuzham
 bu — 2 tbsp tamarind paste + 1.5 cups water\, 2 tbsp sambar powder\, sal
 t\, simmer 10 min\, same temper as sambar. (Short on time: leftover sambar
  works as a substitute.)\nAhana: plain curd rice\, no tempering\, set asid
 e first.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:094ef000-78ab-49e0-9ba2-14f8cd555b20@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260708T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260708T181500
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=WE
SUMMARY:Wednesday Batch Cook — Vegetable Khichdi (Week 1)
DESCRIPTION:NOTE: this slot assumes you're home by 5:45 — most office day
 s you're still commuting (arriving ~6:00)\, so this realistically only wor
 ks on your WFH days\, or if you leave the office early. If it's your week 
 to cook and can't make 5:45\, shift this to whenever you're both home\, be
 fore 6:30 — the recipe doesn't change\, just the clock.\n\nRECIPE — Ve
 getable Khichdi: 1 cup rice + 1/2 cup moong dal\, rinsed together. 3 cups 
 mixed chopped vegetables (carrot\, beans\, peas\, potato). 4.5 cups water\
 , 1/2 tsp turmeric\, 1 tsp cumin seeds\, 1 tbsp ghee\, salt to taste.\nMET
 HOD (Instant Pot): saute cumin in ghee 30 sec -> add rice\, dal\, vegetabl
 es\, turmeric\, salt\, water -> Manual/Pressure Cook 8 min -> natural rele
 ase 10 min.\nAHANA: set aside and mash her portion before adding final sal
 t/chili if any is added at serving.\nThis doubles as tonight's dinner — 
 no separate cooking needed at 6:00.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:63da86a6-48ff-4b0a-9251-66a67ce3f0e6@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260715T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260715T181500
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=WE
SUMMARY:Wednesday Batch Cook — Vegetable Pulao (Week 2)
DESCRIPTION:NOTE: this slot assumes you're home by 5:45 — most office day
 s you're still commuting (arriving ~6:00)\, so this realistically only wor
 ks on your WFH days\, or if you leave the office early. If it's your week 
 to cook and can't make 5:45\, shift this to whenever you're both home\, be
 fore 6:30 — the recipe doesn't change\, just the clock.\n\nRECIPE — Ve
 getable Pulao: 2 cups basmati rice\, rinsed. 2 cups mixed vegetables (peas
 \, carrot\, beans). 1 sliced onion\, 1 tbsp ginger-garlic paste. Whole spi
 ces: 1 bay leaf\, 2 cloves\, 1 small cinnamon stick\, 2 cardamom pods. 2 t
 bsp ghee\, 3.5 cups water\, salt.\nMETHOD (Instant Pot): saute whole spice
 s + onion in ghee 3 min -> add ginger-garlic\, vegetables\, rice\, water\,
  salt -> Manual/Pressure Cook 6 min -> natural release 10 min.\nAHANA: set
  aside and mash her portion before serving with any extra chili.\nDoubles 
 as tonight's dinner.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6e1ead9f-1f65-4ce4-9851-eb75806c028a@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260722T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260722T181500
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=WE
SUMMARY:Wednesday Batch Cook — Dal Khichdi + Roasted Veg (Week 3)
DESCRIPTION:NOTE: this slot assumes you're home by 5:45 — most office day
 s you're still commuting (arriving ~6:00)\, so this realistically only wor
 ks on your WFH days\, or if you leave the office early. If it's your week 
 to cook and can't make 5:45\, shift this to whenever you're both home\, be
 fore 6:30 — the recipe doesn't change\, just the clock.\n\nRECIPE — Da
 l Khichdi: 1/3 cup toor dal + 1/3 cup moong dal + 1 cup rice\, rinsed toge
 ther. 4 cups water\, 1/2 tsp turmeric\, salt.\nMETHOD (Instant Pot): combi
 ne all -> Manual/Pressure Cook 8 min -> natural release.\nRoasted veg (air
  fryer\, cook alongside): 3 cups mixed vegetables (cauliflower\, carrot\, 
 sweet potato) tossed in 1 tbsp oil\, salt\, 1/2 tsp cumin powder -> 400F\,
  15 min\, shake at 8 min.\nAHANA: her portion aside before any final chili
  goes on the khichdi.\nDoubles as tonight's dinner.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:146abeb4-8264-4ef5-bd9e-0f8632bacdf7@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260729T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260729T181500
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=WE
SUMMARY:Wednesday Batch Cook — Lemon Rice + Air-Fryer Tofu (Week 4)
DESCRIPTION:NOTE: this slot assumes you're home by 5:45 — most office day
 s you're still commuting (arriving ~6:00)\, so this realistically only wor
 ks on your WFH days\, or if you leave the office early. If it's your week 
 to cook and can't make 5:45\, shift this to whenever you're both home\, be
 fore 6:30 — the recipe doesn't change\, just the clock.\n\nRECIPE — Le
 mon Rice: 3 cups cooked rice (Sunday's batch\, or fresh). Temper 2 tbsp oi
 l\, 1 tsp mustard seeds\, 1 tbsp chana dal\, 1 tbsp peanuts\, curry leaves
 \, 2 dried red chilies\, pinch turmeric -> mix into rice with juice of 1.5
  lemons\, salt.\nRECIPE — Tofu (air fryer\, cook alongside): 14 oz tofu 
 cubes tossed in 2 tbsp yogurt + 1 tbsp ginger-garlic paste + 1 tsp chili p
 owder + 1/2 tsp turmeric + 1 tsp garam masala + 3/4 tsp salt + 1 tbsp oil 
 -> 400F\, 12 min\, shake at 6 min.\nAHANA: plain rice portion aside before
  the lemon/chili tempering goes in.\nDoubles as tonight's dinner.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ab399eb4-57a4-44f9-8be4-762c9483d799@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
