DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260704T123000
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYDAY=1SA
SUMMARY:Monthly Money Review (1st Saturday)
DESCRIPTION:30 min\, both of you\, nap window. AGENDA: 1) Reconcile account
 s against last month. 2) Confirm every autopay actually fired. 3) Check sa
 vings rate vs. target. 4) Review any open money decisions carried from las
 t month. 5) Log outcome in the Notion Money Reviews database (date\, savin
 gs rate\, decisions made\, anything deferred + a date). Keep it to 30 minu
 tes — this is reconciliation\, not strategy.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e9544014-9a3e-4331-b812-9c9d6fc05a17@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260711T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260711T133000
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTH=4,7,10;BYDAY=2SA
SUMMARY:Quarterly Finance + Career Review (Apr/Jul/Oct\, 2nd Saturday)
DESCRIPTION:90 min\, both of you\, nap window. AGENDA: 1) Portfolio review 
 — allocation drift vs. target\, rebalance if outside bands. 2) Review In
 dia-side accounts\; note any PFIC/FBAR/FATCA questions for the CPA. 3) Tax
 -loss/gain considerations. 4) Insurance check-in. 5) Home-buying gates che
 ck (life stability / financial readiness / market context / house criteria
 ) — still 'not yet' until all four pass\, no re-litigating. 6) Promotion
 -arc checkpoint for both of you — is each quarter's artifact on track\, 
 are the two peak quarters staggered. Log in Notion Money Reviews database.
 \n\nJanuary is the Annual Review instead (half-day) — this quarterly slo
 t does not also fire in January.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
